# Data Dictionary

This document describes the datasets contained in the `data/` directory of this repository.

## Overview

The datasets were collected between February and May 2026 around Koh Tao, Gulf of Thailand, as part of a study investigating the dietary preferences and habitat distribution of Culcita sp. and the effects of elevated Acanthaster sp. densities on dietary selectivity.

---

# CPUE.xlsx

## Description

Contains sightings-per-unit-effort (SPUE) data for Culcita sp. surveys conducted around Koh Tao.

## Purpose

Used to quantify relative abundance between study sites.

## Data type

Raw dataset.

---

# Culcita PITs Data.xlsx

## Description

Contains benthic point-intercept transect (PIT) data used to estimate coral size availability.

## Purpose

Used to calculate coral colony size availability for dietary selectivity analyses.

## Data type

Raw dataset.

---

# Culcita Scars Data.xlsx

## Description

Contains observations of feeding scars associated with individual Culcita sp.

Each line represents observed feeding on a specific coral colony growth form, family and size class. The count collumn indicates the amount of feeding observations on the same combination seen during the survey. 

## Purpose

Used to quantify prey use and calculate dietary selectivity.

## Data type

Raw dataset.

---

# Culcita Habitat Preferences.xlsx

## Description

Contains habitat measurements recorded for individual Culcita sp.

Variables include habitat characteristics such as depth and live coral cover, as well as the precense of scars around the individual.

## Purpose

Used for habitat preference analyses.

## Data type

Raw dataset.

---

# NewData.csv

## Description

Processed ReefCloud annotation dataset.

Contains AI-assisted benthic point-count classifications and manually corrected annotations used to estimate coral availability.

## Purpose

Used to estimate coral family and morphological availability from photo quadrats.

## Data type

Processed dataset.

---

## Missing values

Blank cells indicate that no observation was recorded or that the variable was not applicable.

---

## Coordinate system

Study sites are located around Koh Tao, Gulf of Thailand.

Precise sampling locations have been omitted where appropriate.

